  "observations": [
    "Table: pointer-select Fixture Artist, Shift+Down selects Another Artist too. Return starts First light and appends both artists behind the two initial videos, with exact First/Second/long/Nested order and six queue entries.",
    "After33.18933s Pause, opening one artist only navigates. Fixture/Another/Fixture/\u00c4rtist detail changes show their own actual track names and counts while preserving the same paused First light clock and six-entry queue.",
    "Grid: Fixture Artist plus Shift+Right selects Another Artist. Return appends the same four tracks once, now ten total, and starts the new First light occurrence. The clock advances beyond7s. Normal Quit while playing releases the process with zero error diagnostics/602modules/all source/runtime/fixture/cache guards."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This ordinary run uses the same accepted GUI293/Core265/library282; no production code changed for these journeys. Supplied fixtures are generated silent audio and owned video, not private media.",
    "Sidebar changes are successive observed actions, not proof that native requests overlapped in flight. The pending rapid-query race remains separate. Ordinary classic multi-selection, every sort/filter permutation and full visual/DPI/package acceptance are not established.",
    "Initial queue observation04 precedes animation; settled observation05 supplies the visible drawer. UIA does not expose reliable selected row flags, so actual selection highlights plus the resulting exact queue provide the ordinary selection evidence."
  ],
